# DevSpace's web server (Caddy). deploy/compose.prod.yml sets every {$VARIABLE} below from
# deploy/.env; deploy/compose.local.yml sets them for the local proof (http://app.localhost and
# http://*.ide.localhost, no certificates).
#
#   APP_SITE / IDE_SITE / IDE_BARE_SITE   the site addresses (https://… in production)
#   IDE_BARE_HOST                         the IDE domain itself, which only answers 404
#   IDE_TLS                               cloudflare (wildcard certificate by DNS) or none
#   CSP_CONNECT / CSP_FRAME               the app's WebSocket origin and the IDEs' address pattern
#   API_PORT / IDE_PORT                   the API's two listeners on 127.0.0.1
{
	# No admin API: config changes happen by restarting the container.
	admin off
	email {$ACME_EMAIL}
}

# The IDEs' wildcard certificate comes from Let's Encrypt through Cloudflare's DNS (a DNS challenge
# is the only way to get a wildcard). The token needs Zone - DNS - Edit and Zone - Zone - Read on
# the IDE domain.
(tls_cloudflare) {
	tls {
		dns cloudflare {env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}
		resolvers 1.1.1.1 1.0.0.1
	}
}

# Local proof: plain http, nothing to do.
(tls_none) {
}

(common_headers) {
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		-Server
	}
}

# ---- The app: the API and live updates go to the API, everything else is the web build ----
{$APP_SITE} {
	import common_headers
	encode zstd gzip

	@api path /api/* /socket.io/*
	handle @api {
		# WebSockets (Socket.io) included. The API sees the real client address through
		# X-Forwarded-For (TRUST_PROXY=loopback).
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{$API_PORT}
	}

	handle {
		root * /srv/web
		header Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' {$CSP_CONNECT}; frame-src {$CSP_FRAME}; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'"

		@missingAsset {
			path /assets/*
			not file
		}

		# In this order (route keeps it as written).
		route {
			# A hashed build file that doesn't exist is a 404, not the app's page.
			respond @missingAsset "Not found" 404
			# Any other path is a page of the app (single-page app): serve index.html.
			try_files {path} /index.html
			# Hashed build files never change; index.html must always be fetched fresh.
			header /assets/* Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
			header /index.html Cache-Control "no-cache"
			file_server
		}
	}
}

# ---- The IDEs: every copy has its own address, <copyId>.<IDE domain> ----
{$IDE_SITE}, {$IDE_BARE_SITE} {
	import tls_{$IDE_TLS}
	import common_headers

	# The IDE domain itself serves nothing.
	@bare host {$IDE_BARE_HOST}
	handle @bare {
		respond "Not found" 404
	}

	handle {
		# Host is passed unchanged: the API reads the copy id from it and checks it on every
		# request. The API sets the IDE's own security headers (frame-ancestors, CORP, nosniff).
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{$IDE_PORT}
	}
}
